********  Computer Network Models ********

How network communication betyween two system happens?



So to simplify the tasks and to organize everythng over the network, we use Layer ed Architecture

this layered arch break down all the work into different layers and every layer will be having their own set of tasks and will be performing their own set of work.
And these together will make the data transfer from one device to another over the network.

Layered archotecture : has 2 models 
1.OSI Model
2.TCP/IP Model


ADvantages of layered archtecture:
-Modularity
-Interoperability
-Scalability
-Troubleshooting



OSI Model :
Open System Interconnection

its a theoritical model developed by ISO and it consists of 7 layers

1.Application Layer (UI)
2.Presentation Layer (Tasks around the data)
3.Session Layer (holding session b/w 2 devices)
4.Transpot Layer (dividing data into parts and transport)
5.N/w Layer (some n/w info needs to be embeded)
6.Data Link-layer (manages routing etc)
7.Physical layer (bit data)




TCP/IP Model : backbone of the internet :
Transmission Control Protocol / Internet Protocol

This is a 4 Layer architecture

1.Application Layer - User facing service , follows FTP , http , dns rules etc
2.Transport ayer - responsible for end-to-end coommunication, it uses protocols like TCP n UDP
3.Internet Layer - IP addressing is managed , routing , ARP
4.Network Access Layer  - mac address etc







********  OSI Model ********


OSI model is a set of rules that how different computer systems communicate over network.

developed by ISO - international organization of standardaziation

So OSI model has 7 layers which does independent wkr and together they make communication between two sytems easy.

1.Application Layer
2.Presentation Layer 
3.Session Layer 
4.Transpot Layer 
5.N/w Layer 
6.Data Link-layer 
7.Physical layer


1.physical layer - 

this layer is responsible for actualy physical connection b/w devices.
two devices can connecte via , bluetooth, cabels , internet etc

data will be in forms of bits as compture store in that form.

now this will be transmitting bits from one system to another.

This layer convert data into bits 0,1

functions -
-Bit synchronization
-Bit Rate Control (Transmission rate)
-Connection b/w 2 devices
-Transmission mode



2.Data Link-layer  :

DLL

-> data -> 0101 ..... node --------- node -
                        data,
                        add,
                        mac add


use cases or functions :
-Framing (bits are send in the form of frames)
-Physical Addressing (every device gets a physical address , mac add)
-Error control (if some frames get missed )
-Access Control



3.Network Layer :

Host A  ------------------- Host B
n/w A                           n/w B
so n/w layer is responsible for transfer of data over the n/w


here data is converted into packets which contains the infor about the n/w details like IP address etc

also over n/w a to n/wb it is responsible for routing and ensure shortest route/path also.


Functions : 
1.Routing
2.logical addressing







